            <ArticleTitle>Differential apomorphine effects.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>776-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two dose levels of apomorphine were used with the tail-flick assay. A low dose of apomorphine significantly increased tail-flick latency, whereas a high dose significantly decreased tail-flick latency. Such differential effects have bearing on the reported complex interaction between the dopamine and endorphin systems in the brain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
